# Canada — Provinces & Capitals
# answer-mode: type
# answer-case: insensitive

Capital of British Columbia?
---
Victoria
---
Not Vancouver — Victoria sits on Vancouver Island, and Vancouver isn't on it.

Capital of Alberta?
---
Edmonton
---
Calgary is the bigger city; Edmonton got the capital when Alberta was carved
out in 1905.

Capital of Saskatchewan?
---
Regina
---
Saskatoon is the larger city. Regina was the capital of the old Northwest
Territories before Saskatchewan existed.

Capital of Manitoba?
---
Winnipeg
---
Capital and largest city in one — more than half of Manitobans live there.

Capital of Ontario?
---
Toronto

Capital of Quebec?
---
Quebec City
= Quebec
= Québec
---
North America's only walled city north of Mexico. Montreal is the larger
city.

Capital of New Brunswick?
---
Fredericton
---
Not Saint John (the port city) and not St. John's (that's Newfoundland).

Capital of Nova Scotia?
---
Halifax

Capital of Prince Edward Island?
---
Charlottetown
---
Hosted the 1864 conference that led to Confederation — "the birthplace of
Confederation".

Capital of Newfoundland and Labrador?
---
St. John's
= Saint John's
= St Johns
---
With an apostrophe-s — Saint John (no s) is in New Brunswick.

Capital of Yukon?
---
Whitehorse
---
Dawson City was the gold-rush capital until 1953.

Capital of the Northwest Territories?
---
Yellowknife

Capital of Nunavut?
---
Iqaluit
---
On Baffin Island. Canada's newest capital — Nunavut split from the Northwest
Territories in 1999.

Largest city of British Columbia?
---
Vancouver

Largest city of Alberta?
---
Calgary

Largest city of Saskatchewan?
---
Saskatoon

Largest city of Quebec?
---
Montreal
= Montréal
